  "generated_text": "To find the average (mean) of all 5-digit numbers that can be formed using each of the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7, 8\\) exactly once, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of permutations of the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7, 8\\):**\n\n   The total number of permutations of 5 distinct digits is given by \\(5!\\) (5 factorial):\n   \\[\n   5! = 5 \\times 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 120\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the contribution of each digit to the total sum of all permutations:**\n\n   Each digit will appear in each decimal place (units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands) the same number of times. Since there are 120 permutations and 5 digits, each digit will appear in each place exactly:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{120}{5} = 24 \\text{ times}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the sum of the contributions of each digit in each place:**\n\n   - For the units place, the contribution of each digit \\(d\\) is \\(d \\times 24\\).\n   - For the tens place, the contribution of each digit \\(d\\) is \\(d \\times 24 \\times 10\\).\n   - For the hundreds place, the contribution of each digit \\(d\\) is \\(d \\times 24 \\times 100\\).\n   - For the thousands place, the contribution of each digit \\(d\\) is \\(d \\times 24 \\times 1000\\).\n   - For the ten-thousands place, the contribution of each digit \\(d\\) is \\(d \\times 24 \\times 10000\\).\n\n4. **Sum the contributions of all digits in each place:**\n\n   The sum of the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7, 8\\) is:\n   \\[\n   1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8 = 24\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, the total contribution of all digits in the units place is:\n   \\[\n   24 \\times (1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8) = 24 \\times 24 = 576\n   \\]\n\n   Similarly, the total contribution of all digits in the tens place is:\n   \\[\n   24 \\times 24 \\times 10 = 5760\n   \\]\n\n   The total contribution of all digits in the hundreds place is:\n   \\[\n   24 \\times 24 \\times 100 = 57600\n   \\]\n\n   The total contribution of all digits in the thousands place is:\n   \\[\n   24 \\times 24 \\times 1000 = 576000\n   \\]\n\n   The total contribution of all digits in the ten-thousands place is:\n   \\[\n   24 \\times 24 \\times 10000 = 5760000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Sum the contributions from all places:**\n\n   The total sum of all permutations is:\n   \\[\n   576 + 5760 + 57600 + 576000 + 5760000 = 6400000\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the average (mean) of all permutations:**\n\n   The average of all permutations is the total sum divided by the total number of permutations:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6400000}{120} = 53333.3333\\ldots = 53333 \\frac{1}{3}\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, the final answer is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{53333 \\frac{1}{3}}\n   \\]",
